    "Stigma is a mark of disgrace that sets a person apart and leads others to devalue them. Erving Goffman described how people with a \"spoiled identity\" may hide it to avoid rejection. Public stigma refers to negative attitudes held by the general public; self-stigma occurs when people with a condition accept those attitudes about themselves.",
    "In a hypothetical survey of 1,600 college students who screened positive for depression, researchers measured perceived public stigma toward mental illness and self-stigma, and recorded whether each student used campus counseling during the following semester. Students were also asked whether they had a close friend who had received mental-health treatment.",
