    "Self-stigma was measured with a 10-item questionnaire and split at the median into low and high groups. Counseling use came from center records, which students agreed to share when they joined the study; 92% agreed.",
    "Only about one in three college students with significant depressive symptoms receives treatment in a given year, and stigma is one of the most frequently reported barriers.",
    "Students with high self-stigma who did not use counseling most often said they \"didn't want to be seen as weak.\" Students reported that hearing a friend talk openly about therapy made it seem more normal. Later, the counseling center added drop-in hours labeled \"stress check-ins\" rather than \"mental-health appointments,\" and visits rose 40% the next semester.",
